      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg. Doses above 10 mg aren't recommended, and they raise the risk of significant hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdose can cause prolonged vasodilatory shock. Normal kidney and liver function don't change that limit.\n\nCan you confirm which of these you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the standard maximum. Typical dosing starts at 5 mg and goes up to 10 mg.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily.** This is the usual starting dose.\n3. **30 mg is intended.** If you have a specific reason for this dose, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional and any monitoring you want.\n4. **A different drug or regimen.** Add a second agent if the patient needs more blood pressure control than 10 mg of amlodipine gives.\n\nOnce you reply, I'll enter the order."
      }
     ],
